      "[Kisspeptin](/learn/kisspeptin) is the brain hormone that switches on the reproductive system. It makes the body release its own egg-maturing hormones in a shorter burst. A 2014 study had shown that one injection of kisspeptin-54 could trigger egg maturation in 53 women having IVF.",
